"""Conditional-operator matrix: every when-condition operator at flatten time.

A 6-lane generator where each lane's structure is chosen by a distinct
relational/boolean operator over the loop index i (1..6). Exactly one
when-branch fires per lane, selecting that lane's source:

    i == 1            -> P     (equality)
    i != 1 && i < 3   -> Q     (inequality, less-than, boolean AND)
    i >= 3 && i <= 4  -> P     (ge, le)
    i > 4 || i == 99  -> Q     (gt, boolean OR)

The operators are compile-time only (shdl.md §13, §7.7); they never
become gates. Each lane ORs its chosen source with a shared GND (0) so
OR(src, 0) = src is observable after one cycle. Out (LSB-first) =
[P, Q, P, P, Q, Q].
"""

top component CondMatrix<N = 6>(P, Q) -> (Out[N]) {
    z: __GND__;
    >i[N]{ lane{i}: OR; }

    connect {
        >i[N]{
            when {i == 1}            { P -> lane{i}.A; }
            else {
                when {i != 1 && i < 3}   { Q -> lane{i}.A; }
                else {
                    when {i >= 3 && i <= 4}  { P -> lane{i}.A; }
                    else {
                        when {i > 4 || i == 99}  { Q -> lane{i}.A; }
                    }
                }
            }
            z.O -> lane{i}.B;
            lane{i}.O -> Out[{i}];
        }
    }
}
